<title>GERMANY: Buba's Zeitler says low rates favour home building.</title>
<headline>Buba's Zeitler says low rates favour home building.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bundesbank council member Franz-Christoph Zeitler said on Wednesday low interest rates were favouring Germany's housing construction industry.</p>
<p>Zeitler, who is also president of the regional state central bank of Bavaria, said rates for homes were often less than six percent for five-year debt and less than seven percent for 10-year debt -- levels that should promote construction.</p>
<p>&quot;Low interest rates are due to very favourable refinancing possibilities for banks on the capital market,&quot; he said in prepared remarks for a speech.</p>
<p>&quot;Moderate price developments and efforts to consolidate public budgets have created a favourable interest rate climate,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom + 49 69 756525</p>
</text>
